Make the fixture walk follow symlinks.

`iter_directory` keeps only entries whose `file_type().is_file()`. `walkdir`
does not follow symlinks by default, so for a symlink that predicate is false
and the entry is dropped. Every file Bazel stages in a runfiles tree is a
symlink to the source, so under Bazel the walk finds nothing and the harness
reports an empty run rather than a failure -- 620 fixtures silently not tested.

`follow_links(true)` makes `file_type()` report the target's type. Under Cargo,
where the fixtures are real files, it changes nothing.

Applied through `crate.annotation` in //MODULE.bazel rather than vendored, so
Cargo keeps using the released crate unmodified. Upstream would take this as a
one-line change; until then it lives here.

--- a/src/data_source.rs
+++ b/src/data_source.rs
@@ -75,6 +75,7 @@
 
 fn iter_directory(root: &Utf8Path) -> impl Iterator<Item = std::io::Result<TestEntry>> + '_ {
     walkdir::WalkDir::new(root)
+        .follow_links(true)
         .into_iter()
         .filter(|res| {
             // Continue to bubble up all errors to the parent.
